{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777522210,"nonce":"siK1r+jCoRxL6EJxAWeYZ6mVM8k=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABA5fgjw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/111","origin":"github"},"title":"nav: define lever-arm/base_link contract for SBG and mavros position streams","message":"## Summary\n\nBoth the SBG `ekf_nav` and the mavros `global_position/raw/fix` streams\npublish position at their respective GNSS antenna locations, **not at\n`base_link`**. Any consumer that treats either stream as \"the boat's\nposition\" is silently picking up a metre-class lever-arm error in vehicle\nbody frame, plus a yaw-rotation-coupled error in world frame. We need a\ndeliberate decision about where lever-arm correction happens, and a\nconsistent contract for what each topic is supposed to report.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSame 2026-04-29 in-water cross-check used for the URDF gap issue:\n\n- Body-frame offset SBG − MAV (moving): forward **−0.635 m**, port +0.020 m,\n  vertical +0.024 m (after geoid).\n- World-frame horizontal std 0.628 m vs body-frame std 0.119 m — proof\n  the offset is body-fixed, i.e., a real lever arm.\n- Vertical residual after geoid is 24 mm and uncorrelated with roll/pitch\n  (r = +0.005 / −0.063), so the lever arm is essentially horizontal.\n\n## Reading\n\n- **mavros side**: ArduPilot publishes the primary GPS antenna position\n  through MAVLink. It does not lever-arm-correct to the EKF origin /\n  base_link by default. `EK3_GPS_OFFS` and `GPS_POS1_X/Y/Z` are the\n  parameters that affect this on the FCU side.\n- **SBG side**: the Ellipse-D's lever-arm parameters live in sbgCenter\n  (Sensor → Aiding → GNSS → Lever arm). If they are set to the\n  IMU-from-antenna offset, `ekf_nav` outputs at the IMU; if they are\n  zero, it outputs at the antenna. We do not currently have these\n  values captured in version control or the deployment notes.\n\n## Proposed scope\n\nDecide and document:\n\n1. **Where each stream should report** — at `base_link` (then both can be\n   consumed interchangeably), or at the actual antenna with explicit TF\n   relationships (then consumers must apply TF). Pick one and state it.\n2. **Where the correction happens** — three options:\n   - **On-sensor**: ArduPilot `EK3_GPS_OFFS` + `GPS_POS1_*` set; SBG\n     lever-arm in sbgCenter set. Pros: every consumer downstream sees\n     base_link directly. Cons: harder to audit, has to be re-applied if\n     hardware changes, lives outside the repo.\n   - **In a small bridge node**: subscribe to the raw antenna-frame\n     topic, look up TF, republish at `base_link`. Pros: configuration is\n     in the repo, easy to tweak. Cons: extra topic, extra latency, extra\n     thing to drift from the URDF.\n   - **In each downstream consumer**: every node that wants base_link\n     position does its own TF lookup. Pros: minimal surgery. Cons: easy\n     to forget; bugs are silent (current state).\n3. **Capture and version-control** the SBG lever-arm + alignment config\n   so the URDF + sbgCenter config + ArduPilot params don't silently\n   diverge.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Documented contract for what `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/ekf_nav`,\n  `/bizzy/mavros/global_position/raw/fix`, and `/bizzy/odom` are\n  reporting (frame + reference point + datum).\n- Body-frame SBG − MAV horizontal offset on a follow-up deployment\n  should drop into GPS-CEP territory (sub-decimetre under good fix)\n  rather than being a steady 0.64 m.\n- SBG roll/pitch/yaw alignment captured somewhere in version control\n  (likely the URDF, see #110) so the +1.79° roll isn't rediscovered\n  next year.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Modelling the SBG geometry in the URDF — see the URDF gap issue.\n- Datum/altitude convention (the +31 m geoid offset is a separate\n  concern; flag if it actually trips up a consumer).\n\n## References\n\n- Deployment-day cross-check writeup: `docs/logs/2026/2026-04-29_dev_logs.md`\n  (timeline entry 2026-04-30T00:06-04:00).\n- Source bag: `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/2026-04-29T21-43-29+00-00`.\n\nPart of #104.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}